def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    doc = prefix.document_ids[-1]
    token = prefix.token_bytes[-1]
    text = prefix.token_strings[-1]
    if carry is None or carry[0] != doc:
        opening, repeated, history = token, True, b''
    else:
        opening = carry[1]
        repeated = carry[2] and token == opening
        history = carry[3]
    carry = (doc, opening, repeated, (history + token)[-48:])
    if repeated:
        return carry, opening_value(text)
    if history == b'{' and text == '[':
        return carry, 3.32
    if history == b'//\n' and text == '//':
        return carry, -1.07
    if text.strip() in {'page', 'pages'}:
        if history.lower().rstrip().endswith(b'this preview shows'):
            return carry, 0.45
    if '\ufeff' in text:
        return carry, -0.65
    if text == '\x00':
        return carry, -0.06
    return carry, -0.045 if text.strip() == '•' else 0.0

programs.haiku:
"""Layer 1, MLP down-projection, component 3813: a document-opening detector.

What it does, in plain terms: this component speaks almost only at the very start of a
document. There, attention can see nothing but the first token, so its value is a fixed
function of that token's identity. The value is kept while the document keeps repeating
that same first token (for example a long run of carriage returns at the top of a file).
Everywhere else it is near zero.

Value by first token, roughly:
  - the line-comment token '//' followed by a newline (top of a source file): 13;
  - HTML '<!', carriage return, NUL, bullet '•', 'void': about 6;
  - 'int', 'char', 'string', 'class', 'def', '##', end-of-text, escaped quote: about 2.5;
  - other code and markup openers ('#', '/*', docstring quotes, '<?', 'package', 'const'): about 1.5;
  - 'import' and a bare '//', and a few single capital letters: slightly negative;
  - digits and capitalised words (names, titles): about 0.3 to 0.5;
  - any other document opener: about 0.3, roughly the average first token.
