"""An orthographic m-fragment detector.

The main positive spelling is German 'mit' (and 'damit'). Short mang,
mitt and mv fragments also excite it. Mood is strongly negative. Across a
split after m, it/ith/ite and y-continuations tend positive, whereas oo, ow,
ew and ell continuations tend negative. Full words containing these letter
sequences are not indiscriminately treated as fragments. MathML's mfrac/mrow,
Python's mro, 'all manner', repeated middle dots and document-opening 'Title:'
are separate
